    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Brice Turang** (73.40) and **Jose Caballero** (69.59) headline our optimal lineup, largely driven by elite stolen base upside against exploitable matchups. **Brice Turang** benefits from a massive 18% SP skill boost against Cade Povich, and despite a slight platoon penalty, his leadoff placement and the high likelihood of an aggressive base-running environment secure his position as our primary engine. Meanwhile, **Jose Caballero** represents the high-water mark for situational leverage; his matchup against Eduardo Rodriguez yields a 13% platoon boost, and the slow delivery profile of the opposing starter gives him a 2% bump in SB potential, effectively mitigating the penalty of his assumed #9 spot in the order. **Corbin Carroll** (67.03) and **Mickey Moniak** (66.10) also project as high-ceiling plays, with **Corbin Carroll** specifically thriving on the 85% SB efficiency window provided by the opposing battery, keeping his total output well within the \"Strong\" start tier despite facing a capable arm in Gerrit Cole.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision landed on **Austin Riley** (56.69), who finished just shy of supplanting **Travis Bazzana** (56.93) for the MI/3B utility slots. While **Austin Riley** carries a solid projection, the optimizer favored **Travis Bazzana** due to a significantly better SP matchup and the benefit of a 7% platoon advantage, which provided the necessary margin to edge out the veteran. Elsewhere, we remain cautious regarding the overall lineup volatility, as nearly every position player is currently listed as \"Lineup Pending.\" Specifically, **Gabriel Moreno** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** are anchored by projected order spots that, if shuffled downward by team management, could see their scores dip toward our 50-point threshold. Additionally, while **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains in our lineup for his 14% platoon advantage, the daunting assignment against Paul Skenes serves as a primary risk factor that necessitates close monitoring before first pitch.",
